CrewDispatch third-party notices
===========================

CrewDispatch's own source and build output are licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0; the complete product license is shipped separately as LICENSE. The
`private: true` package flag only prevents accidental npm publication and does not
change that license. This file records third-party copyrights and license texts for
material bundled with the install payload and for behaviour rewritten or adapted
from earlier projects. It is a notice file, not a legal opinion, and it does not
replace either CrewDispatch's LICENSE or any third-party license.

The installer copies this file unchanged to <install-root>/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES and
records its SHA-256 in the install marker. The installed package also carries the
unmodified upstream LICENSE file of every bundled npm package at the paths listed in
section 2. The auditable payload inventory is maintained in the canonical development
records and is reviewed before release.

