1. Material adapted or rewritten from earlier projects
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1 wb-crew — MIT (Copyright (c) 2026 WorkBuddy Crew contributors)

Parts of CrewDispatch's behaviour (CLI discovery and Windows spawn handling, NDJSON
stream parsing and exit classification, durable job store and generation registry,
process-tree cancel, MCP tool surface, wake notification, model selection,
rate-limit downgrade handling, Hub settings and retention policy) were rewritten in
TypeScript - and in places adapted - from a read-only inspection of a private
`wb-crew` installation supplied to the project owner. Internal provenance records
retain the inspected file hashes and behavior mapping. No file from that installation
is copied verbatim and no file in it was written to during that work.

